            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal modifies the summary and context quotes to incorporate paragraph (5)'s general limitation on civil litigation materials. However, that limitation is already retained as a separate record (C0007). Under the governing instructions, a condition retained in another record is not to be incorporated into this statement, making the edit unnecessary.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The draft reading for C0000 is independently complete, accurately reflecting the statutory requirement in subsection (d)(1) without omitting required conditions or misrepresenting the discretionary written statement exception for accompanying persons. Leaving it unchanged is correct.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The edit inaccurately converts a discretionary agency option regarding accompanying persons ('except that the agency may require the individual to furnish a written statement authorizing discussion of that individual’s record in the accompanying person’s presence') into a mandatory requirement applicable to all individuals whether accompanied or unaccompanied. It also unnecessarily imports paragraph (5), which is already retained in another record.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
